With the change in Gehennom to the open style caverns I find teleport
control to be pretty valuable in zipping through the levels on the way
down to avoid getting surrounded.  With the open style levels, the
increased monster generation frequency, and increased monster hp (or
so it seems) it sometimes feels like two monsters engage me in the
time it takes to slash through one.  IME it very often doesn't pay to
melee in Gehennom; though I do kill dragons for their scrolls, potions
and scales.

Also with the game shortcuts available with controlled levelports I
use teleport control quite a bit.  Also in Sporkhack I set up a stash
level (but typically not in Vanilla) and thus need teleport control to
get back to my stash.

Limiting the range might be interesting but I do like the new
difficulty associated with not being able to teleport while carrying
the amulet.  It takes an extra move to get away now since one has to
drop the amulet _first_ and then teleport away from danger.

Consider also that allowing a limited range teleport might make
getting back across the moat and firetrap ring at the vibrating square
too trivial. :)

Just some thoughts from my experience, FWIW


